WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.300
Your lists hold dozens of tasks.

00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:05.224
In the morning, you only want to see what
matters today.

00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:11.441
Merkzettel groups every list by due date:
overdue, today, tomorrow, this week,

00:00:11.491 --> 00:00:13.190
later, and tasks without a date.

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:19.440
The smart lists look across all your
lists.

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:21.481
Planned shows everything with a due date.

00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:27.382
Important collects every task you starred.

00:00:31.350 --> 00:00:32.813
Now pick today's tasks.

00:00:33.113 --> 00:00:35.748
Hold Control and click the tasks you want
to do today.

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:43.020
The sun button in the selection bar adds
them to My Day.

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:45.851
For a single task, press Control and T.

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:53.287
My Day now shows exactly the tasks you
chose for today.

00:00:57.350 --> 00:01:00.241
Tick off what you have done, with the
check box or with Control and D.

00:01:05.350 --> 00:01:07.161
My Day starts empty every morning.

00:01:07.461 --> 00:01:10.352
Unfinished tasks stay in their lists, with
their due dates.

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:18.639
My Day is stored on this computer only,
because Microsoft does not offer it to
other

00:01:18.689 --> 00:01:19.889
apps.

00:01:23.350 --> 00:01:25.173
That is how you plan your day with
Merkzettel.

